{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And the flesh of the bull.</b> It mentions 'flesh' because he dismembers it without flaying, and afterward takes it out and burns it. And regarding the bull of the anointed priest it is written 'he shall take out the entire bull,' because he takes it out whole and dismembers it outside. So too our Sages expounded." "<b>It shall be burned with fire.</b> Rashi: we do not find an outer sin-offering that is burned except this one. But this is difficult, for we find the calf of Aaron in the section of Shemini, and the second bull of the Levites in the section of Beha'alotekha, and the twelve goats of a sin-offering in Ezra, and the bull of the future in Ezekiel — all of which are outer sin-offerings that are burned. And some give a reason why the sin-offerings of the investitures and the sin-offering of Shemini that is for investiture were burned: since they are the priest's own offerings, just as we find with the meal-offering of a priest — 'it shall be whole.' Another reason why this is burned, as Scripture itself explains: <b>it is a sin-offering</b> — this gives the reason why it is burned, because it comes for purification of the altar, as it is written 'and you shall purify the altar.' And the purification is not completed except with the blood, so at the time of slaughter it is as though the altar were not yet there, and it is as though it went outside, where it is not eaten."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {0 "The text has (שמנחתו) [שמנתחו] — a correction from 'its meal-offering' to 'he dismembers it,' reflected in translation. The parallel correction (ומנחתו) [ומנתחו] likewise."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:08.927185903Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}